      "evidence": "Street schedule transcribed from Luton Borough Council's own PDF 'Roads within the selective licensing area' (titled 'Selective licensing South ward (old boundary)', Private Sector Housing team, July 2023), linked from luton.gov.uk/housing/private-tenants-homeowners-landlords/landlords/selective-licensing; 'old boundary' refers to the pre-2023 South ward boundary, which now corresponds to the Town Centre and Park Town areas. 102 roads, 95 'All numbers' and 7 with house-number/flat restrictions transcribed verbatim. Dates: the designation (https://www.luton.gov.uk/sites/default/files/migrated/Housing/Lists/LutonDocuments/PDF/licensing/selective-licensing/selective-licensing-designation-oct-23.pdf) was made 25 October 2023 with a nominal commencement of 5 February 2024 and ceases 4 February 2029; the council's page states the scheme was delayed by a long appeal and 'went live on 1 June 2026'. Both recorded dates are therefore CORRECT, but note the end date was not extended, so the scheme runs only ~2 years 8 months."
